{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-ezk-9-1","title":"Ezekiel 9:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 A vision, whereby is shewn the preservation of some; 5 and the destruction of the rest. 8 God cannot be intreated for them.</p>\n<p>cried. 43:6,7; Isa 6:8; Am 3:7,8; Re 1:10,11; 14:7 Cause. Ex 12:23; 2Ki 10:24; 1Ch 21:15; Isa 10:6,7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-9-2","title":"Ezekiel 9:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>six. Jer 1:15; 5:15-17; 8:16,17; 25:9 the higher. 2Ki 15:35; 2Ch 27:3; Jer 26:10 lieth. Heb. is turned. slaughter weapon. Heb. weapon ofhis breaking in pieces. and one. 10:2,6,7; Le 16:4; Re 15:6 ink-horn.{Keseth,} (in Chaldee, {kista,} Syriac, {kesto,} Ethiopic, {kasut,}) denotes a bottle, or vessel to hold any fluid; and being here united to {sophair,} a writer, is not improperly rendered as an ink-horn: so one of the editions of Aquila, [melandocheion,] and Vulgate, {atramentarium.} Dr. Shaw informs us, that among the Moors, \"the {Hojas,} i.e., writers or secretaries, suspend their ink-horns in their girdles.\"</p>\n<p>by his side. Heb. upon his loins. beside. Ex 27:1-7; 40:29; 2Ch 4:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-9-3","title":"Ezekiel 9:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>3:23; 8:4; 10:4; 11:22,23; 43:2-4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-9-4","title":"Ezekiel 9:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>set a mark. Heb. mark a mark. Ex 12:7,13; Mal 3:16; 2Co 1:22; Eph 4:30; 2Ti 2:19; Re 7:2,3; 9:4 Re 13:6,7; 14:1; 20:4 that sigh. 6:11; 2Ki 22:13,19,20; Ps 119:53,136; Isa 57:15; Jer 13:17 2Co 12:21; 2Pe 2:8,9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-9-5","title":"Ezekiel 9:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>hearing. Heb. ears. 1Sa 9:15; Isa 5:9; 22:14 Go. 10; 5:11; 7:4,9; 8:18; 24:14; Ex 32:27; Nu 25:7,8; De 32:39-42 1Ki 18:40</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-9-6","title":"Ezekiel 9:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>utterly. Heb. to destruction. old. Nu 31:15-17; De 2:34; 3:6; Jos 6:17-21; 1Sa 15:3; 2Ch 36:17 but. Ex 12:23; Jos 2:18,19; 6:22-25; 2Ti 2:19; Re 7:3; 9:4; 14:4 and begin. 8:5-16; Jer 25:29; Am 3:2; Lu 12:47; 1Pe 4:17,18 at the. 8:11,16; 11:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-9-7","title":"Ezekiel 9:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>7:20-22; 2Ch 36:17; Ps 79:1-3; La 2:4-7; Lu 13:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-9-8","title":"Ezekiel 9:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>that I. Nu 14:5; 16:4,21,22,45; De 9:18; Jos 7:6; 1Ch 21:16; Ezr 9:5 Ah. 4:14; 11:13; Ge 18:23; Jer 4:10; 14:13,19; Am 7:2-5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-9-9","title":"Ezekiel 9:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>The iniquity. 7:23; 22:2-12,25-31; De 31:29; 32:5,15-22; 2Ki 17:7-23 2Ch 36:14-16; Isa 1:4; 59:2-8,12-15; Jer 5:1-9; 7:8,9; Mic 3:9-12 Zep 3:1-4 and the land. 8:17; 2Ki 21:16; 24:4; Jer 2:34; 22:17; La 4:13,14; Mt 23:35-37 Lu 11:50 full of. Heb. filled with. perverseness. or, wresting ofjudgment. 22:27-29; Mic 3:1-3; 7:3,4 The Lord hath. 8:12; Job 22:13; Ps 10:11; 94:7; Isa 29:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-9-10","title":"Ezekiel 9:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>mine. 5; 5:11; 7:4; 8:18; 21:31,32 but. 7:8,9; 11:21; 22:31; De 32:41; 2Ch 6:23; Isa 65:6; Ho 9:7; Joe 3:4 Heb 10:30</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-9-11","title":"Ezekiel 9:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>reported the matter. Heb. returned the word. I have. Ps 103:20; Isa 46:10,11; Zec 1:10,11; 6:7,8; Re 16:2,17</p>"}]}